A Power Platform solution is normally exported as a .zip. Git/source control works better with individual files, 
so PAC CLI can unpack the ZIP into folders/files that Git can track.

First export your solution:
    pac solution export --name BudgetApproval --path "BudgetApproval.zip"
Then unpack it:
    pac solution unpack --zipfile "BudgetApproval.zip" --folder "BudgetApproval"

you'll have a folder containing the solution's individual files/components.
You can then:
  Add those files to Git/Azure DevOps
  Track who changed what
  Compare versions
  Maintain development history
  Later pack those files back into a solution ZIP: and import the solution.
